To validate the TES and TER calculation, the reciprocal of \(Q_{\text{T}}^{\text{fit}}\) and \(Q_{\text{T}}^{\text{dist}}\) are first convoluted with the output of the Particle\(\oplus\)Geant framework - the reconstructed \(E_{\text{T}}\) distributions of the simulated \(\pi^{0}\) and \(\gamma\), labeled \(E_{\text{T}}^{\text{reco}}\left[\Delta E_{\text{T}}^{\text{trg}}|\pi^{0}, \gamma\right]\) (where \(\Delta E_{\text{T}}^{\text{trg}}\) indicates the bin of measured \(E_{\text{T}}^{\text{trg}}\)) - to yield the distributions \(\tilde{E}_{\text{TF,D}}^{\text{reco}}\left[\Delta E_{\text{T}}^{\text{trg}}| \pi^{0},\gamma\right]\), where the subscripts F and D indicate whether \(E_{\text{T}}^{\text{reco}}\) was convoluted with the either the **fit** to or the whole **d**istribution of \(Q_{\text{T}}^{\text{trg}}\):

Figure 12.4: Unweighted input \(E_{\text{T}}^{\text{sim}}\) vs. unweighted output of the clusterizing algorithm (12.4a), and their ratio (12.4b).

