These back-smeared distributions are then compared against the \(E_{\text{T}}\) distributions of the simulated \(\pi^{0}\) and \(\gamma\) matched to reconstructed BEMC clusters, \(E_{\text{T}}^{\text{match}}\left[\Delta E_{\text{T}}^{\text{trg}}|\pi^{0}, \gamma\right]\). The distributions \(E_{\text{T}}^{\text{reco}}\), \(\tilde{E}_{\text{T}}^{\text{reco}}\), and \(E_{\text{T}}^{\text{match}}\) are shown in figure 12.6.

By back-smearing \(E_{\text{T}}^{\text{reco}}\) with \(Q_{\text{T}}^{\text{fit}}\), the peaks of the \(E_{\text{T}}^{\text{match}}\) distributions are successfully recovered in \(\tilde{E}_{\text{T}}^{\text{reco}}\). Furthermore, back-smearing \(E_{\text{T}}^{\text{reco}}\) with \(Q_{\text{T}}^{\text{dist}}\), the entire \(E_{\text{T}}^{\text{match}}\) distributions are successfully recovered, thus validating the TES and TER calculation. Now the weights to be applied to the simulation may be calculated with confidence.

