where \(\Delta_{\text{F,D}}^{\text{Py8,Py6}\star}\) are the weights corresponding to the data back-smeared with \(Q_{\text{T}}^{\text{fit}}\) and \(Q_{\text{T}}^{\text{dist}}\) respectively. In total, there are twenty-four sets of weights corresponding to the three bins of measured \(E_{\text{T}}^{\text{trg}}\), the two trigger species, the two simulation samples, and the two choices of \(q_{\text{T}}^{\text{trg}}\) distributions for convolution. Figure 12.7 shows \(\tilde{E}_{\text{TF}}^{\text{meas}}\) versus \(E_{\text{T}}^{\text{Py8}}\) and \(E_{\text{T}}^{\text{Py6}\star}\), and figure 12.8 the corresponding sets of weights.

